# Vampires Bot Project Structure

This is a Telegram bot built with aiogram for managing political districts and actions.

## Core Architecture

- **Main Entry Point**: [app.py](mdc:app.py) - Bot application startup and configuration
- **Configuration**: [config.py](mdc:config.py) - Application configuration management
- **Database Config**: [db/config.py](mdc:db/config.py) - Database connection configuration
- **Database Session**: [db/session.py](mdc:db/session.py) - SQLAlchemy session management

## Key Directories

- `routes/` - Bot command handlers and routing
- `middlewares/` - Middleware components (timing, user registration)
- `screens/` - UI screen components and templates
- `templates/` - Jinja2 message templates (Russian localization)
- `db/` - Database models and operations
- `services/` - Business logic services
- `keyboards/` - Inline keyboard components
- `states/` - FSM (Finite State Machine) states
- `text_handlers/` - Text message handlers
- `options/` - Configuration options system
- `utils/` - Utility functions
- `alembic/` - Database migrations

## Database Models

The bot uses SQLAlchemy with the following main models:
- `users` - User information and registration
- `districts` - Political districts
- `actions` - Political actions and activities
- `politicians` - Politician data
- `news` - News articles
- `user_scouts_districts` - User-district relationships

## Docker Setup

- [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) - Multi-service Docker setup with PostgreSQL
- [Dockerfile](mdc:Dockerfile) - Bot container definition
- [docker-entrypoint.sh](mdc:docker-entrypoint.sh) - Container startup with migrations
- [DOCKER.md](mdc:DOCKER.md) - Complete Docker documentation

## Environment Configuration

- [.env.docker](mdc:.env.docker) - Docker environment template
- [.env](mdc:.env) - Local environment configuration
- [config.py](mdc:config.py) - Configuration loading and validation